How it is included
------------------
The tree is vendored as-is and inert: it is NOT part of the npm workspaces of
the host repository (it lives in vendor/, outside the apps/* workspace glob, and
is not in the host package-lock.json), it is not built by the host CI or deploy, and no install or lifecycle script is run
for it. To run it, work inside this directory in a separate checkout.

Modifications from upstream
---------------------------
1. src/i18n/dict/es/**        New Mexican Spanish (es-MX) UI dictionaries,
                              built from the English dictionaries (key = Chinese
                              original text, as in the other locales).
2. src/i18n/locale.ts         Added locale 'es' (document language es-MX,
                              system-language detection, stored-locale check,
                              agent language name "Spanish (Mexico)").
3. src/i18n/dictRegistry.ts   Added the 'es' dictionary branch (falls back to
                              English for untranslated entries, like 'it').
4. README.es-MX.md            New Mexican Spanish README (summary).
5. README.md                  One line: link to README.es-MX.md.
6. NOTICE                     This file.

Everything else is byte-identical to the upstream commit above. Because
OpenChatCut is AGPL, any modified version made available to users over a
network must offer its corresponding source; the changes listed here are in
the git history of the host repository.
